# re-exercise after CLAUDE.md edits (no regression) + confirm the gate still lets normal work through
bash .tools/hooks/tests/test_never_rules_gate.sh 2>&1 | tail -3
echo ""
cat > /tmp/gatemsg.txt <<'EOF'
build(NEVER-GATE): F-009 + F-010 + the ungated bare-terraform-apply -- ONE PreToolUse hook, LIVE, exercised in-harness. And RV-0047's premise is FALSE: there is no terraform shim.

MSTR RV-0047: "every gate RV-0046 declared a blocker was RULED AND NEVER BUILT. Not disputed,
not descoped -- ruled, agreed, and left. 581 commits happened in between." Correct, and this
closes three of them with one mechanism.

=== FIRST: RV-0047'S PREMISE IS FALSE, AND SO IS CLAUDE.md's ===
RV-0047 F-009 says: "No `git` PATH shim -- and the `terraform` shim it was modeled on EXISTS at
.tools/terraform. The mechanism is proven; it simply was not applied to git."

    $ file .tools/terraform
    .tools/terraform: PE32+ executable for MS Windows 6.01 (console), x86-64, 8 sections

THERE IS NO TERRAFORM SHIM. It is the real Go binary. Same for .tools/terraform.exe. The "proven
mechanism" was inferred from a FILENAME. CLAUDE.md NEVER#7 says the same thing in its own text
("same mechanism as the bare-`terraform apply` shim: one shim, two NEVER rules") -- so the claim
was written into the rulebook and then read back by MSTR, and by me, as evidence it existed.

*** A COMMENT IS A CLAIM WITH NO VINTAGE AND NO TEST. *** I landed that doctrine into Rule 22a two
hours ago (off CTO~B's finding on dispatch:396-400) and it immediately caught the review that was
sequencing my own work. Fourth instance in one night.

AND IT HAS A SECOND CONSEQUENCE NOBODY DREW: .tools/ is on PATH and .tools/terraform IS the real
binary -- so a bare `terraform apply` (NEVER#3) has been running STRAIGHT THROUGH, ungated, this
whole time. TWO NEVER rules unenforced, and the doc cited a shim for one as the model for the other.
Neither existed. NEVER#3 was not even on the overdue list -- nobody knew it was open.

=== WHAT I BUILT: ONE HOOK, THREE GATES ===
.tools/hooks/never-rules-gate.sh -- PreToolUse, matcher Bash|PowerShell.
The mechanism that IS proven here is the PreToolUse hook (block-bare-inbox-watch + comp-tool-hud,
both live). And it is STRICTLY BETTER than the PATH shim MSTR wanted: CLAUDE.md itself notes the
bash `git()` shadow is useless because "PowerShell never sources ~/.bashrc, so BOTH forms are
ungated there." A hook has no shell. It fires on both.

  GATE 1 (NEVER#7, F-009) -- rebase on a SHARED branch: `git rebase`, `git pull --rebase`, AND a
    BARE `git pull` when pull.rebase=true. That is ALL FOUR CELLS, including the one CLAUDE.md
    says "nobody types and nobody gated" -- the one the remedy for a rejected push sends you to.
    Scoped to CLOUD/DEV/PROD/main/master; a scratch-branch rebase is the author's own business.
    Honours `git -C <path>` so a portal command is judged against PORTAL's branch.
  GATE 2 (NEVER#3) -- bare `terraform apply`/`destroy` (skips safe-apply's HALTGT checkpoint, the
    drift-plan check, and the paired-permission lint).
  GATE 3 (LD-0276, F-010) -- `git commit`/`safe-commit` with `-m` AND a backtick or $(. The
    substitution happens in the SHELL before git or safe-commit sees the arg, so a safe-commit lint
    STRUCTURALLY cannot catch it (CVO source-proved this). Only a raw-.tool_input.command hook can.

  Audited override on all three: append `# never-override: <reason>` -> org/git-author-override-audit.log.

=== THE TRAP, AND THE CONTROL THAT PROVES I AVOIDED IT ===
CLAUDE.md REFUSES a text deny-rule for rebase, and it is right: "the matcher fires on MENTIONS, so it
would forbid every brief and commit message discussing rebase -- INCLUDING THE ONE REPORTING THIS."

Solved by matching the SUBCOMMAND POSITION, never the word: `git [opts] rebase` matches; `git commit
-m "...never rebase..."` cannot, because the token after `git` is `commit`. Text-matching is correct
in GATE 3 and ONLY there -- precisely because -F moves the body OUT of the shell-parsed argument.

EXERCISED 22/22 (.tools/hooks/tests/test_never_rules_gate.sh), and THE NEGATIVE CONTROLS ARE THE
POINT: a commit message MENTIONING rebase -> PASS. `grep -rn "rebase" CLAUDE.md` -> PASS. The
prescribed remedy `git pull` (merge) -> PASS. `git pull --no-rebase` -> PASS. `terraform plan` ->
PASS. safe-apply -> PASS. If N1-N11 ever go red the gate ships OFF: a gate that blocks the brief
documenting the hazard is worse than no gate -- it will be disabled, and it will have punished the
person doing the right thing.

=== LIVE, NOT CONFIGURED (Rule 22a -- a config read is not a behavioural claim) ===
Wired into .claude/settings.json, then EXERCISED THROUGH THE REAL HARNESS with a probe chosen so a
DEAD gate would be harmless (`git rebase --help` -- matches the rule; prints help if unenforced):

    $ git rebase --help
    BLOCKED (CLAUDE.md NEVER#7): rebase on the SHARED branch 'CLOUD' ...

It DENIED a real Bash tool call, this session. NEVER#7 has been "almost entirely on your discipline"
by its own admission; it is now enforced.

CLAUDE.md updated: NEVER#3 + NEVER#7 now state the gate, and record that the shim they cited never
existed. The old "3 OF 4 CELLS UNENFORCED" text is kept, not deleted -- the reasoning still teaches.

KNOWN OVER-BLOCK, stated: `git rebase --help` is denied (harmless, and it is what let me prove the
gate live). Not worth complicating the matcher for; erring toward deny on rebase is correct.

CLOSES: F-009, F-010, and NEVER#3 (which was open and unlisted). NOT closed: F-001's safe-apply
two-record INTENT/OUTCOME audit -- that is the next build.

